    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1300</span><span class="rf-text">Ile-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ife">Ife</a>, the sacred city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a>, is at its height; its artists cast naturalistic heads in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> alloy</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">17th century</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> rises to dominate the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> lands; its kings honour Shango, the orisha of thunder, remembered as one of their predecessors</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1830s</span><span class="rf-text">The collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> and the wars that follow send many enslaved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">Early 19th century</span><span class="rf-text">African priestesses found Casa Branca, one of the first great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/candomble">Candomblé</a> houses, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahia">Bahia</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1993</span><span class="rf-text">The Supreme Court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> upholds the right of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santeria">Santería</a> church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> to practise animal sacrifice</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2005</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> proclaims Ifa divination a masterpiece of humanity’s oral heritage; the sacred grove of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osogbo">Osogbo</a> becomes a World Heritage Site</span></li></ol>
